-The comparison with Ada varies across working points. At 10~dB Ada has lower LPIPS and DreamSim and higher CLIP-I, whereas NeST has higher PSNR. Ada also has higher CLIP-I at 4~dB and slightly lower DreamSim at 19~dB. NeST's PSNR gains over Ada are 4.116/0.455/1.226~dB at 4/10/19~dB. All 1500 evaluated transmissions per SNR succeed for NeST, WHOLE, and Ada, so their overall and success-conditioned means coincide (Supplement~S2).
+At 4~dB, NeST achieves mean LPIPS/DreamSim of 0.263/0.184, compared with 0.395/0.243 for Ada. At 10~dB Ada has lower LPIPS and DreamSim and higher CLIP-I, whereas NeST has higher PSNR. At 19~dB NeST has lower LPIPS, while Ada has slightly lower DreamSim. Ada also has higher CLIP-I at 4~dB. NeST's PSNR gains over Ada are 4.116/0.455/1.226~dB at 4/10/19~dB. All 1500 evaluated transmissions per SNR succeed for NeST, WHOLE, and Ada, so their overall and success-conditioned means coincide (Supplement~S2).
 
 On the fixed 100-source control set, replacing Ada's sampled tail with argmax increases both LPIPS and DreamSim at $N=512$, 4/10~dB and $N=1024$, 10~dB; all six paired intervals exclude zero (Supplement~S3). Thus sampling gives the stronger perceptual baseline at these tested points.
 
